  policyRelevance: [
    "The negative coefficients on political globalization in social democratic and Southern European welfare states after 2008 likely reflect the EU's response to the sovereign debt crisis — the European Semester, the Fiscal Compact and a strengthened Stability and Growth Pact — rather than a general globalization effect. Greece and Portugal had conditional lending programmes, Italy and Spain were subject to surveillance, and the result was welfare retrenchment across the region.",
